        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Sagrajas</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">23 October 1086 (Friday, 12 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajab">Rajab</a> 479 AH); Muslim sources say <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> had agreed to fight on the Monday</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The plain of Zallaqa or Sagrajas, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a> near the present border of Portugal, in the west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mutamid-ibn-abbad">Al-Mu'tamid ibn Abbad</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>, with ten thousand Almoravid cavalry in the vanguard and 4,000 black troops among the Almoravids; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI of Castile</a> with allies from Aragon and elsewhere, his army put at 60,000</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Muslim forces won and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> fled by night to Coria. The sieges of major Andalusian cities were lifted, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a>'s standing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> rose.</span></div>
